From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:31:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] windows.devices.enumeration: read-only enumeration of audio
 and removable devices, watcher, access

DeviceInformation.FindAllAsync (all, by class, by AQS filter), CreateFromIdAsync and
GetAqsFilterFromDeviceClass work over the audio capture and render endpoints (their
device interface identifiers) and removable drives; classes with no device here and
filters that cannot be evaluated give an empty DeviceInformationCollection. DeviceInformation
(Id, Name, IsEnabled, IsDefault, an empty Properties map) and its collection with iteration
are real objects. DeviceWatcher keeps its status (Created, Started, EnumerationCompleted,
Stopped) and reports the existing devices through Added and EnumerationCompleted on a
thread-pool thread, which holds no reference on the watcher object; Updated and Removed
handlers are kept. DeviceAccessInformation validates its arguments and keeps its handlers.
All objects answer GetIids, GetRuntimeClassName and GetTrustLevel. Removes the todo_wine
marks that now pass.

